the-firm-as-one-program-lines-9 : List (List Word)
the-firm-as-one-program-lines-9 = cons "- **C1** Prove any provable property of the whole firm ([P2], [P6], [P7])." (cons "  The firm can ask any question about itself and receive a proof in place of an estimate. Whether any sequence of exchange events, across every strategy and gateway, can push exposure in a name past its limit is a type over the composed fleet. Today such questions are answered by sampling: tests, simulations, monitoring and post-mortems. In one program they are answered for every run at once." (cons "- **C2** Research and production are one definition run in two worlds ([P6], [P7])." (cons "  A strategy is one definition run under two handlers: a historical world and the live one. The feature computed in research is the same content-addressed object computed in production, and any difference between simulated and real fills is a stated relation instead of a ghost discovered in the profit and loss. What a researcher proves about a signal carries to the deployed artifact through the source-to-machine relation, on a processor through C or on an FPGA." (cons "- **C3** Compute and knowledge accumulate instead of being redone ([P8], [P9])." (cons "  A result computed once is a result for everyone who asks the same question, valid exactly as long as its recorded reads still hold. Large shares of research clusters now spend their cycles recomputing results that already exist somewhere unrecognized; that spending ends. More importantly, a relationship one researcher establishes becomes a construction others build on without re-establishing it and without fear that it means something different in their context." (cons "- **C4** The fast path is a specialization that carries its proof ([P5], [P7])." (cons "  The hot path from packet to order is a specialization of verified definitions, carrying its proof. When the fast path cannot be broken by changing it, it can be changed as freely as research code, and the specialists who guard it become authors of specializations that apply everywhere at once. See [PE]." (cons "- **C5** Risk bounds are invariants of the whole composed system ([C1], [P6])." (cons "  The paper's order ledger bounds filled position plus admitted outstanding orders and proves the bound over every admissible sequence of exchange events, including the interval during a rollout (§10.10). That is the SEC's market access rule, 15c3-5, established as a theorem of the running system in place of a check performed system by system. Knight Capital lost about 440 million dollars in 45 minutes on 1 August 2012 because one of eight servers kept old code behind a repurposed flag. In one program the version on each server is a content identity, a flag that means two things in two versions is two different objects, and the rollout's invariant is proved over every interleaving. That failure cannot be constructed." (cons "- **C6** Exact reasoning under partial observation, and the value of information can be computed ([P1])." (cons "  A market maker never sees the true state of the market; it sees its fills, the public book and the tape. The fiber of states compatible with those observations is the exact object its decisions should rest on, and an action is safe when it is safe for every state in that fiber. Because refining an observation shrinks the fiber, the value of a new data source becomes computable: it is how much that source shrinks the fibers on which decisions depend. Data purchased today by intuition can be priced before it is bought." (cons "- **C7** Exchange changes and new venues propagate ([P4], [P10])." (cons "  A venue's protocol and matching rules are definitions. When an exchange changes its packet format, the change flows through the parser's proof, the specialized parser, the native artifact and a rollout in which old and new formats run side by side. A new venue or asset class, such as a new crypto exchange, a prediction market or a newly opened foreign market, is integrated by writing its definition once, after which everything composes with it." (cons "- **C8** Audit trails and compliance are queries over retained effect histories ([P8])." (cons "  The audit trail is the effect history the evaluator already keeps, since its semantics forbids losing or replaying an issued effect. A regulator's question is a query over the information space answered with evidence." (cons "- **C9** Debugging restricts the set of runs compatible with what was observed ([P1])." (cons "  When something goes wrong, the debugger restricts the set of runs compatible with what was observed, holding missing packets as unknowns, and finds the cause in minutes while the strategy would otherwise sit switched off." (cons "- **C10** AI researchers at any scale, because their output is checked, not trusted ([P11])." (cons "  Every firm now tries to use AI models for research and engineering and hits the same limit: their output cannot be trusted, so human review is the bottleneck. When a claim is a construction the machine checks, an AI agent's strategy either satisfies the risk invariant or it does not, and its faster hot path either carries its proof or does not ship. The firm can run ten thousand artificial researchers, their output joining the information space as safely as a person's, each building on everything already established. Research capacity stops being a headcount and becomes a compute budget." (cons "- **C11** Acquired systems and vendor software come in by equivalence and lifting ([P3], [P4])." (cons "  When a firm acquires a team or a company it inherits systems built on different models of the same things, and integration takes years. An equivalence between the acquired representation and the firm's own carries operations, data and proofs across together. Vendor software, from order management to analytics, is lifted as data, and its outputs carry relations the firm checks instead of trusting." (cons "- **C12** The provenance of every running byte is known ([P9])." (cons "  Every definition is identified by content, every change is a new object with its author and rationale, and nothing is overwritten. An unauthorized change is a different identity that cannot silently replace the approved one, so the integrity of the firm's code against insiders and compromised dependencies becomes a property it can check." (cons "- **C13** Contracts, clearing and margin are rules over states ([P2], [P6])." (cons "  Master agreements, clearing obligations, margin terms, exchange membership rules and data licences are rules over states. A margin call is a transition, a clearing obligation is an effect with a scope, a collateral agreement is an invariant, and whether a strategy respects a data licence is a property that can be proved. The firm knows at every moment what it owes and to whom, and legal review stops being the slowest step into a new market." (cons "- **C14** Exchange semantics are definitions the firm can reason about ([P4])." (cons "  The firm can also reason about a matching engine's order types and priority rules as precisely as about its own code, so edge that comes from the exchange's rules is found by construction instead of by accident." (cons "- **C15** Network and FPGA are targets of the same program ([P7])." (cons "  Firms have spent hundreds of millions on microwave and laser links to send information along the shortest path physics allows between Chicago and New Jersey. The network, the switches, the FPGA and the custom silicon are processes with transition semantics, and latency is an observation of them. With strategy, network and circuit in one program, the firm optimizes the whole path instead of each component in its own vocabulary, and a strategy can be specialized into a verified circuit in days." (cons "- **C16** Knowledge belongs to the firm, not to individuals, and onboarding is a walk ([P2], [P9])." (cons "  What a person understood becomes a definition with its rationale, still valid when they go home and still valid when they leave. Key-person risk, and much of what garden leave and non-competes pay for, comes from the firm being unable to separate knowledge from the person. A new hire walks the firm's information space in order, as an agent walks this repository, and becomes productive in days instead of most of a year." (cons "- **C17** Disagreements resolve on a presented shared basis ([P1], plus common ground)." (cons "  Two portfolio managers who disagree do so because at least one of them lacks something the other has. When the system presents the shared basis, the facts, models and constraints both accept and the exact point where their inferences part, the disagreement resolves on evidence instead of politics. A firm of brilliant, competitive people loses an enormous amount to internal friction, and that loss shrinks. The work is derived from the science of human happiness: connection, purpose and shared understanding are what people need, and an information space with its ignorance removed provides them." (cons "" nil))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
